1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,610
Good evening, excellence.

2
00:00:01,610 --> 00:00:03,310
9 a.m.… the manager

3
00:00:03,310 --> 00:00:05,010
has just walked in.

4
00:00:05,030 --> 00:00:07,185
An employee stops the manager at the door:

5
00:00:07,185 --> 00:00:09,340
we have a problem with a client’s order.

6
00:00:09,340 --> 00:00:10,920
The manager says: leave it with

7
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:12,500
me… I’ll get back to you.

8
00:00:12,530 --> 00:00:15,770
10 a.m.: another employee, another problem.

9
00:00:15,770 --> 00:00:16,750
Leave it with me.

10
00:00:16,750 --> 00:00:18,730
12 noon: a third one.

11
00:00:18,730 --> 00:00:19,800
Leave it with me.

12
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:22,125
By the end of the day… the manager

13
00:00:22,125 --> 00:00:24,450
is drowning, and the whole team is waiting.

14
00:00:24,450 --> 00:00:26,540
In 1974,

15
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:28,196
Oncken and Wass wrote a

16
00:00:28,196 --> 00:00:29,520
Harvard Business Review article

17
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:31,500
called: “Who’s Got the Monkey?”

18
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:33,090
Every problem… is a monkey.

19
00:00:33,090 --> 00:00:34,157
And every time you say

20
00:00:34,157 --> 00:00:35,010
“leave it with me”…

21
00:00:35,010 --> 00:00:36,838
the monkey jumps from the

22
00:00:36,838 --> 00:00:38,300
employee’s shoulder onto yours.

23
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:39,620
That’s the difference I

24
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:40,940
asked about last episode.

25
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:43,510
Dumping: hand over the task… and disappear.

26
00:00:43,510 --> 00:00:45,350
Delegating: hand over the task,

27
00:00:45,350 --> 00:00:47,190
the authority, and follow up…

28
00:00:47,190 --> 00:00:49,400
and final accountability stays with you.

29
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:51,830
Before you delegate, ask three questions.

30
00:00:51,830 --> 00:00:53,960
What result is needed… and by when?

31
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:55,410
What authority do they have?

32
00:00:55,410 --> 00:00:57,720
When and how will we follow up?

33
00:00:57,720 --> 00:00:58,720
Try it tomorrow:

34
00:00:58,720 --> 00:01:00,245
when someone brings you a problem,

35
00:01:00,245 --> 00:01:01,770
don’t say “leave it with me.”

36
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:03,350
Say: what do you suggest?

37
00:01:03,350 --> 00:01:04,700
Leave the monkey on their

38
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:06,050
shoulder… but stay beside them.

39
00:01:06,050 --> 00:01:09,243
The EFQM Model sees excellent leadership as

40
00:01:09,243 --> 00:01:11,980
empowering people… not carrying for them.

41
00:01:11,980 --> 00:01:13,310
A great manager isn’t the

42
00:01:13,310 --> 00:01:14,640
one carrying all the monkeys…

43
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,467
it’s the one whose team knows

44
00:01:16,467 --> 00:01:17,990
how to raise its own.

45
00:01:17,990 --> 00:01:20,065
What if a free gift showed

46
00:01:20,065 --> 00:01:22,140
you exactly where you go wrong…

47
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:24,030
yet most companies resent it and

48
00:01:24,030 --> 00:01:25,920
rush to get rid of it?

49
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:27,050
What do you think it is?

50
00:01:27,050 --> 00:01:28,280
Tell me in the comments.

51
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:29,480
Save this episode, and

52
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:30,680
see you next time

53
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:32,510
on Masaa Al-Tamayoz.
